/grid "420px 1fr" {

  /region --bg #282828 --padding 1.5rem {
    /code polyester {
      ## Why Polyester?

      /columns 3 --gap 2rem {
        /card --icon rocket {
          ### Fast
          Compiles to HTML instantly.
        }

        /card --icon shield {
          ### Familiar
          If you know Markdown...
        }

        /card --icon bolt {
          ### Powerful
          Layouts, theming, highlighting.
        }
      }
    }
  }

  /region --padding 3rem --margin 2rem {

    ## Why Polyester?

    /columns 3 --gap 2rem {
      /card --icon rocket {
        ### Fast
        Compiles to HTML instantly. PDF via Chrome.
        Zero runtime overhead.
      }

      /card --icon shield {
        ### Familiar
        If you know Markdown and Slack , you know Polyester.
        Commands are just `/slash` syntax.
      }

      /card --icon bolt {
        ### Powerful
        Layouts, theming, code highlighting.
        Full control over your documents.
      }
    }

  }

}

/grid "420px 1fr" {

  /region --bg #282828 --padding 1.5rem {
    /code polyester {
      ## The Syntax

      /code polyester {
        /text "Hello" --bold --color blue
      }

      /code polyester {
        /columns 2 {
          /card { Left side }
          /card { Right side }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  /region --bg #f8fafc --padding 3rem {

    ## The Syntax

    Write documents with Markdown, supercharged with `/commands`.

    /columns 2 --gap 3rem {

      /region {
        ### Basic Command

        /code polyester {
          /text "Hello" --bold --color blue
        }

        Commands start with `/`, take arguments and flags,
        and optionally contain blocks with `{ }`.
      }

      /region {
        ### Blocks & Nesting

        /code polyester {
          /columns 2 {
            /card { Left side }
            /card { Right side }
          }
        }

        Nest commands freely. Markdown content
        flows naturally between them.
      }

    }

  }

}

